---
description: Keep Slack DMs draft-only and require confirmation for channel posts
alwaysApply: true
---

# Slack Outbound Messages

Never send or schedule a direct message. Create or update an unsent DM draft instead, even when the user confirms the text, says it is urgent, or grants standing permission.

Before sending or scheduling a channel message or thread reply:
1. Show the exact final text and destination.
2. Ask the user to confirm.
3. Wait for a new user reply approving that exact post.

The initial request to send, urgency, standing permission, or "don't ask again" is not confirmation. If the text or destination changes, confirm again.

Creating or updating an unsent Slack draft does not require confirmation.
